story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years from 1951 to 2025 on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids. October to November came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025 January to February ran 53% of normal and April to May ran 144%. So far in 2026 March to April came in at 21% of normal, and every grid had its driest year in 2001.</p>"}
